[statement]
`a` needs `lib<2` and `b` needs `lib>=2`; one package holds a name, so apk
refuses, though each requirement alone has a version that meets it.
Contrast `requirements-no-package-meets-together`, which shows the same
through a name packages provide.

[repository]
P:a
V:1
D:lib<2

P:b
V:1
D:lib>=2

P:lib
V:1

P:lib
V:2

[request]
a
b

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
| ERROR: unable to select packages:
|   lib-1:
|     breaks: b-1[lib>=2]
|     satisfies: a-1[lib<2]
refused
